. 
. * F11: all result presentation lives here, out of wooldid_worker (which is ne
> ar stata's
. * per-program compiled-size ceiling), reading ONLY e() - the live estimation 
> path and
. * replay (wooldid typed alone after estimation) both call this, so their outp
> ut is
. * identical by construction. non-eclass on purpose: ereturn inside a non-ecla
> ss program
. * is a hard error, so this program is structurally incapable of altering the 
> posted
. * results. part(1) = header through the adversarial lines; part(2) = subgroup
>  tables
. * through the pairwise comparisons (split so the eclass wooldid_ptp call can 
> stay in
. * the caller between them); part(roth) redisplays the Roth diagnostics from e
> (roth_*)
. * on replay without re-running the quadrature.
. * NFFAST-02: rename CFX matrix row stripes from margins' tempvar-embedded sub
> names
. * (e.g. "1bn.__000ABC" - volatile every run) to stable lattice_# keys, and nu
> ll the row
. * equations. lives outside wooldid_worker (compiled-size ceiling). the lattic
> e level is
. * read from the matrix's own row subnames - no r() capture (margins' r(by#) i
> s not a
. * documented stored result). validation guarantees nonnegative integer levels
> , so the
. * generated names are always valid; a parse failure is loud, never silent
. cap prog drop wooldid_cfxstripe

. prog def wooldid_cfxstripe
  1. version 16.0
  2.   args cfxm
  3.   local rn : rowfullnames `cfxm'
  4.   local newnames
  5.   foreach rtok of local rn {
  6.     local rsub `rtok'
  7.     if strpos("`rtok'", ":") > 0 local rsub = substr("`rtok'", strpos("`rt
> ok'", ":") + 1, .)
  8.     if !regexm("`rsub'", "^([0-9]+)(bn|b|o)?\.") {
  9.       dis as error "Error: wooldid could not parse the CFX matrix row name
>  '`rtok'' into a lattice level; please report this."
 10.       error 498
 11.     }
 12.     local newnames `newnames' lattice_`=regexs(1)'
 13.   }
 14.   matrix rownames `cfxm' = `newnames'
 15.   matrix roweq `cfxm' = _
 16. end

